Title:
GapMap — Execute PIC payloads from .text section alignment padding in loaded system DLLs

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
GapMap is a Windows x64 proof-of-concept that maps and executes a position-independent (PIC) payload from the zero-filled alignment padding (“tail gap”) at the end of the `.text` section inside already-loaded System32 DLLs. It leverages the fact that PE sections are page-aligned (0x1000), leaving unused bytes that are still mapped and inherit the section’s page protections—often `PAGE_EXECUTE_READ` for `.text`. The tool scans loaded system DLLs, finds the largest executable `.text` tail gap, temporarily flips protection to `PAGE_READWRITE` to copy the payload, restores the original protection, and starts execution via `CreateThread` from within the DLL’s `.text` address range. This provides an execution location inside a trusted module’s executable mapping without leaving pages RWX in the final state. It’s mainly useful for red teamers, malware developers, and researchers exploring in-memory code placement, module stomping variants, and integrity/detection edge cases. The repo also discusses detection angles like `VirtualProtect` monitoring and HVCI/CI page-hash behavior on page-in.

Technical Focus:
- PE section/page alignment and `.text` tail padding (VirtualSize vs page mapping)
- In-memory payload placement inside loaded signed system DLL mappings
- Memory protection transitions (`VirtualProtect` RW flip and restore)
- PIC payload execution via `CreateThread`
- Detection considerations: API hooking, CI/HVCI page hashing, disk-vs-memory comparisons

Use Cases:
- Execute shellcode/PIC payloads from executable padding within legitimate DLL mappings
- Research EDR detections around `VirtualProtect` and non-standard code locations
- Evaluate integrity-checking gaps (hashing only up to `VirtualSize` vs full page)
- Develop/compare alternative injection primitives (module padding vs classic module stomping)

Keywords:
Windows x64, PE format, section alignment, page alignment, .text section, VirtualSize, System32 DLL, in-memory injection, shellcode, PIC payload, CreateThread, VirtualProtect, PAGE_EXECUTE_READ, PAGE_READWRITE, module mapping, code cave, alignment padding, HVCI, Code Integrity (CI), EDR detection